From: misc-de <misc-de@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 14:50:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mixer-control: Every port takes the new profiles of its card

update_card() replaces the card's profiles, gvc_mixer_card_set_profiles()
frees the old ones. A port's list of profiles was renewed only through
update_ui_device_on_port_changed(), that is only for a port with a UI
device. A Bluetooth headset's hands-free port has none (it is not
offered on its own), so its list kept pointing at freed profiles.

The next stream update asked whether the stream's port is the hands-free
one and read those profiles: Phosh crashed (SIGSEGV in g_str_has_prefix)
when a headset connected or switched between music and hands-free.

Take the new profiles for every port of the card.
---
 gvc-mixer-control.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

--- a/gvc-mixer-control.c
+++ b/gvc-mixer-control.c
@@ -2729,6 +2729,12 @@
 
                         if (g_strcmp0 (card_port->port, port->name) == 0) {
                                 found = TRUE;
+                                /* gvc_mixer_card_set_profiles() above freed the card's old
+                                 * profiles. A port without a UI device (a headset's hands-free
+                                 * port) gets no new list from update_ui_device_on_port_changed(),
+                                 * so take the new profiles here for every port */
+                                g_list_free (card_port->profiles);
+                                card_port->profiles = determine_profiles_for_port (port, gvc_mixer_card_get_profiles (card));
                                 update_ui_device_on_port_changed (control, card_port, port, card);
                         }
                 }
